# macOS HIG — Savitar 2

Full reference: [docs/HIG.md](../../docs/HIG.md). Follow Apple [Settings HIG](https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/settings) for app-level settings.

## Settings window checklist

- One modeless **Settings** window; **Settings…** in app menu (**⌘,**)
- **No** Save / Cancel / Apply — changes apply and persist immediately
- Close button only; fixed size unless pane has scrollable content
- Multiple groups → `NSToolbar` with `.preference` style (macOS 11+); title = active pane name
- Dismiss with **Escape** or **⌘+.**
- Use `NSWindow.configureAsSettingsWindow()` and `fitContentSize(_:centerIfNeeded:)`

## Controls

- Gray out unsupported options with a tooltip (do not hide)
- Use "Settings" terminology on macOS 13+, not "Preferences"
- World-specific options → World Settings sheet, not app Settings

## When adding UI

1. Check [docs/HIG.md](../../docs/HIG.md) and [docs/Stories.md](../../docs/Stories.md)
2. Match existing AppKit patterns in `client/Savitar2/src/views/`
3. Prefer system controls, Auto Layout, and standard shortcuts
